{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>One portion taken from the fifty, and you shall give them to the Levites</b> etc. Since the Levites took ten per thousand, the priests took one portion corresponding to them, for they were but one of eleven divisions within the families of Levi. How so? The families of Levi are five and a half: the Libnite and Hebronite, the Mahlite and Mushite, the Amramite, and half of Izhar, as explained in the section of Pinchas. And the Amramite family was half priests and half Levites. Thus the priests are one of the eleven divisions within the families of Levi." "<b>From the cattle, from the donkeys, and from the sheep.</b> And if you ask: why did HaShem not command to take a levy from the camels, when there were many camels there, as it is written in the war of Gideon — ולגמליהם אין מספר? One may answer: Scripture mentioned only those from which they took a levy, and they did not take a levy from an unclean animal — only from the donkeys, since they were consecrated through the firstborn of a donkey. But HaShem said, as it is written, ומכל הבהמה — which implies yet another species of animal, such as camels."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "ומכל הבהמה (Num 31:28, not 31:30) — cited by Chizkuni without specifying; left unaddressed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:26.437038008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}